   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "Is there a reason to check by wtxid and not txid? If there's an orphan with the same txid but different witness, we still evaluate the package here even though it can't get into the mempool.",
   "request": "",
   "status": "answered",
   "status_by": {
    "at": "2026-11-03",
    "by": "instagibbs",
    "id": "rc:4458593056",
    "quote": "yes you're correct, and this would also cover the case where a different wtxid enters through p2p, which the current fix misses."
   },
   "status_note": "author agreed that checking by txid is correct and covers different wtxid entering via p2p",
   "type": "objection",
